# Navigation architecture — current

## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are authoritative. This file supersedes the old fixed workspace-first IA rules.

## Authority

- Backend/domain responses use semantic `NavigationTarget`; they never encode Next routes as product semantics.
- Web URL/router state may select Web details, but it is presentation/platform state, not domain authority.
- Reusable stores/controllers must not treat Next route strings as cross-platform identity.
- Direct deep links must remain recoverable without depending on browser history.

## Current Web

Preserve working route behavior unless the assigned issue explicitly changes it. Existing Messages/Work/Projects/Vimla/Settings routes are implementation reality, not a permanent final IA.

New Channels/Groups/communication features may not be placed into old navigation solely because this file once prescribed a fixed sidebar.

## Final Web navigation

Final placement, hierarchy and responsive composition are owner-driven after #122 Web Functional Complete. #123 Design Freeze then normalizes the approved presentation.

Until then:
- implement required functionality with coherent temporary/current Web placement;
- do not invent fake destinations for unimplemented features;
- do not make backend contracts depend on temporary placement;
- feature gates remain authoritative.

## Desktop / Mobile

Desktop begins only after #123 and may reuse finalized Web DOM presentation.

Mobile is a separate native presentation phase after Desktop. It may have different navigation composition while using the same semantic NavigationTarget and client/domain state.

Do not encode “mobile bottom nav must be exactly X/Y/Z” as a permanent domain rule before the owner design/native phase approves it.
